#!/usr/bin/env python3
# SPDX-License-Identifier: GPL-2.0-or-later
"""p10-enter: bring a UC-P10 from its running OS into U-Boot fastboot, then
RAM-boot an installer image with `fastboot boot`.

NOT FOR USE ON A UNIT until the Opus review that P10-ENTER.md asks for and the
owner's approval. The rockusb route writes the misc BCB (a rule-9 write).

  p10-enter ssh --target USER@HOST --image IMG --sha256 HEX --expect-serialno S [options]
      The unit runs mainline. Read only over ssh: the restart block and the
      tsx-autoupdate fields (no install, no hold), and LBA 49156 (dd, decoded
      here: the next slot must be successful). Then `/usr/sbin/uc-pxx-reboot
      fastboot` (the register route, it writes nothing). The tool writes
      nothing to the unit.

  p10-enter rockusb --image IMG --sha256 HEX --expect-serialno S
                    --bcb-go HEX --expect-ab-sha256 HEX --go-file FILE [options]
      The unit is in the stock download mode (rockusb). The tool reads the A/B
      sector (LBA 49156, read only; the next slot must be successful, the
      other slot successful too or never tried (trying {prio below the next
      slot's, tries 7, succ 0}: a stock unit whose other slot never booted),
      and its first 32 bytes must have the given sha256) and the BCB (LBA
      49184, 4 sectors),
      writes the BCB command "bootonce-bootloader" when the command field (BCB
      bytes 0..31, to the first NUL) is empty or an unrecognised leftover that
      U-Boot ignores, skips the write if that command is already set, and stops
      if a boot-recovery/boot_recovery is pending (exit 29; it must not be
      overwritten), reads it back, resets the unit and waits for fastboot.

  p10-enter dump [--log-dir DIR]
      Read only. The unit is in the download mode. Saves the primary GPT (LBA
      0..33), the factory data block (LBA 3666944, 8 sectors; private, mode
      0600, never to be sent: it holds the MAC), the A/B sector and the BCB,
      prints where the GPT has misc and cfg, the model of the factory data,
      the sha256 of the others and if the BCB is a known state.

--model ucp10|ucp8 (ssh, rockusb): the model of the unit and of the image
(UC-P8.md). The image's own device tree must name that model, before any
command. On the rockusb route the tool also reads the primary GPT and the
factory data block (read only) before the A/B sector: misc must be at LBA
49152 (8192 sectors) and cfg at LBA 3666944, and the factory data must name
the model by the rule of the stock U-Boot ("UC-P8" in the first 5 bytes, else
"UC-P10" in the first 6), with a valid checksum. Otherwise nothing is written.
One case is not a stop: a factory read that gives only 0xCC bytes (all 4096).
The U-Boot download mode gives that for the LBA (it does not serve it;
measured on a UC-P10, DLMODE.md 8.1). It is not data of the unit, so the host
has no model then. The tool logs that, and the model gate is the RAM image's
(it reads cfg itself before any write) and the image check above. Any other
block (also one with only some 0xCC bytes) must name the model, as before.

Then (ssh, rockusb): the fastboot serial and `getvar serialno` must be the
given one; single getvars (never `getvar all`) must give the same A/B state as
the sector read before; `fastboot boot` of a checked copy of the image.

Guards (see P10-ENTER.md): LBA 49156 is only read; every command is checked at
the one place where programs start (Runner.check_exec); no timeout or kill of
any device command; SIGINT, SIGTERM, SIGHUP and SIGQUIT are held to the next
safe point; the log file is written before the terminal, and a dead terminal
does not stop the sequence; Maskrom = stop; --dry-run runs no program.
"""

